    {
      "ordinal": 8,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "4.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "The sources provide the following available materials during the Middle Ages:\n\n● linen,\n● wool,\n● silk,\n\n● coton.\n\nThose materials are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nDepending on the area and time-period, other textiles fibers may be available. Any other material based on historical sources can be accepted.\n\nTextiles were used in many applications, such as:\n\n● tabard,\n\n● covering a coat of plates, corazzina or brigandine,\n● gambesons,\n\n● chausses,\n\n● helmet decoration (burlet, torse, orle, crest etc.).",
      "page_from": 4,
      "page_to": 4,
      "stable_key": "textile-and-leather:4.1",
      "parent_key": "textile-and-leather:4",
