      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "5.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "The sources provide a numerous amount of information about the use of leather. Leather can be decorated or not.\n\nThe use of leather is Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\nLeather was used in many applications, such as:\n\n● covering a coat of plates, corazzina or brigandine,\n● gambesons,\n\n● helmet element (suspension system, straps etc.),\n● belts,\n\n● pouches,\n\n● shoes,\n\n● etc.\n\nReproduction of a medieval shoes - 1300/1350 - Archeologisch Museum Haarlem\n\nLeather glove - 1450/1470 - Metropolitan Museum of Art",
